        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the inpatient treatment of your 67-year-old female patient, admitted on 17/03/2013 due to an acute exacerbation of known COPD. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Physical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed the exacerbation. Blood tests showed mild systemic inflammation. Spirometry supported obstructive ventilatory impairment consistent with her known diagnosis. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, resulting in clear clinical improvement. Vital signs remained stable throughout the stay. Prior to discharge, patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided. We recommend continuation of her regular inhaled therapy and close outpatient follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>"
            },
